33% is not considered probable (since 0.33 < 0.333), then only 2400 in B is probable. But 2400 in A is not probable (since 100% is not > 1.0). So both have only one probable outcome (2400), same value. So average is same. Thus, the reason would be indifferent. Therefore, the reason can be applied, but it leads to indifference. However, the rule says 'prefers the lottery with a higher average of probable outcomes'—if equal, it is indifferent. So the reason is applicable, but does not favor either lottery.",
